# Updated: 2026.10.11
# Based on https://raw.githubusercontent.com/blackmatrix7/ios_rule_script/master/rule/Clash/Cloudflare/Cloudflare.list and https://raw.githubusercontent.com/blackmatrix7/ios_rule_script/master/rule/Clash/Cloudflarecn/Cloudflarecn.list

# 1. Shared hosting, content delivery, and third-party-site assets.
# Custom domains are handled by specific rules above or by the IP fallback below.
# Only DNS hosting at Cloudflare does not imply HTTP traffic uses Cloudflare IPs.
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,cloudflareinsights-cn.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,cf-ipfs.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,cloudflare-ipfs.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,cloudflareapps.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,cloudflareinsights.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,cloudflarepreview.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,cloudflarestorage.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,cloudflarestream.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,pages.dev
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,trycloudflare.com
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,videodelivery.net
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,workers.dev
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,r2.dev
DOMAIN-SUFFIX,imagedelivery.net

# 2. Cloudflare shared-IP fallback. Keep below ALL specific website/application domain rules.
# no-resolve is intentionally removed so unresolved hostnames can reach this fallback via DNS.
# This does not change your DNS settings; the full DNS/TUN configuration was not supplied.
# Do not interpret this as exhaustive identification of every Cloudflare customer/service.
# Source: https://www.cloudflare.com/ips/ (reviewed 2026-10-11).
# Source: https://wiki.metacubex.one/config/rules/
